From 0b95c36f74bd4b32656760eca5ac31d5fc538542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Holly <lee.j71@northeastern.edu>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:00:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add a std::format fallback so csrc builds with GCC 11

The Ascend A3 training image ships GCC 11 only, has no network, and no
g++-13 in its apt sources, so <format> (GCC 13+) is unavailable. csrc uses
std::format in five places, all with bare {} placeholders and no format
specs, so a small fallback covers them.

format_string is aliased through type_identity_t to keep Args a non-deduced
context, matching libstdc++; without that every log::write call site fails
to deduce Args from the format-string literal.

This is a toolchain workaround for the 910C container, not intended for
upstream -- the README requires GCC >= 13.

(cherry picked from commit d9db5d2e8490a10f07c004b064aa81c5bc6480ac)
---
 csrc/engine/scheduler.hpp    |   7 ++-
 csrc/utils/format_compat.hpp | 112 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 csrc/utils/log.hpp           |   7 ++-
 3 files changed, 120 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 csrc/utils/format_compat.hpp

